                                        "description": {
                                            "__typename": "JobDescription",
                                            "html": "\u003Cp>\u003Cb>Job Overview\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>As a Design Engineer \u002F Mechatronics Engineer at HandsOn Robotics, you have the unique opportunity to play an integral role in the development of one of the first robot-based automation products for large-scale commercial kitchens. From your first day on the job, you will be a significant member of our early core team located in Dresden, in the heart of Europe. By designing innovative robotic automation systems and integrating advanced robotics solutions, you will directly contribute to bringing our products to life and helping our customers keep their businesses running efficiently. Are you ready to embrace this challenging role, contribute to the construction of a successful robotics company, and grow together in the most exciting times we&rsquo;ve seen in robotics?\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cb>Your Contribution\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Shaping the product throughout the entire development cycle: from the idea to commissioning at the customer's site\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Designing individual parts, assemblies and entire products\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Product planning and customization, including integration into the overall system\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Repair and testing activities, including directly at the customer's site\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cb>Your Profile\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Degree in mechatronics, mechanical engineering, automation technology\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>or Technician qualification in mechatronics, mechanical engineering\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>or Completed vocational training as an industrial mechanical\u002Fmechatronic technician with advanced knowledge\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Knowledge of design \u002F CAD is essential\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Basic knowledge of the Machinery Directive and the application of standards is an advantage\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Desirable: basic knowledge of electrical engineering, electronics, circuits and automation\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Structured way of working and initiative\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Enjoy interdisciplinary cooperation\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>English language skills spoken and written\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Professional experience is not necessarily required, but graduates with a focus on practical work are also an alternative (HandsOn mentality should be in the foreground)\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cb>Compensation, Benefits and Perks\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>The primary work location is Dresden, with the option for part-time home office based on individual arrangements\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>From 45,000&euro; annual pay\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>30 days of paid vacation\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Full-time (37.5h) and part-time employment possible\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Be part of an open and motivating work atmosphere where your ideas are valued\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>You are welcome to contribute to the full mission, from tech details up to strategic decisions\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Thrive in a high-impact, flat-hierarchy working environment with fast decision-making\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Embark on a pioneering developer journey with limitless learning and growth opportunities\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cb>About HandsOn Robotics\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>HandsOn Robotics automates manual activities in industrial processes through the use of robot technology with the support of AI. Initially, our focus is on the automation of manual activities in large-scale catering. Filling jobs that are unattractive due to the physically strenuous, monotonous and repetitive tasks and low pay poses enormous challenges for our customers, which we meet with robot-supported automation products. Become part of the HandsOn Robotics team and help us to make the process in hospitals and university catering resilient and future-proof.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cb>Apply now\u003C\u002Fb>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>If you are ready to build a truly progressive automation company in the heart of Europe and want to play a key role in our team, we look forward to receiving your application! No matter if in German or English &ndash; please send us your CV, relevant work samples and optional recommendation letters to the following email address:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>jobs@handson-robotics.de\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Looking forward to hearing from you!\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Art der Stelle: Vollzeit, Festanstellung\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Gehalt: ab 45.000,00&euro; pro Jahr\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>Arbeitszeiten:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>Montag bis Freitag\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>Arbeitsort: Vor Ort\u003C\u002Fp>",
                                            "text": "*Job Overview*\n\nAs a Design Engineer \u002F Mechatronics Engineer at HandsOn Robotics, you have the unique opportunity to play an integral role in the development of one of the first robot-based automation products for large-scale commercial kitchens. From your first day on the job, you will be a significant member of our early core team located in Dresden, in the heart of Europe. By designing innovative robotic automation systems and integrating advanced robotics solutions, you will directly contribute to bringing our products to life and helping our customers keep their businesses running efficiently. Are you ready to embrace this challenging role, contribute to the construction of a successful robotics company, and grow together in the most exciting times we’ve seen in robotics?\n\n*Your Contribution*\n\n•\tShaping the product throughout the entire development cycle: from the idea to commissioning at the customer's site\n\n•\tDesigning individual parts, assemblies and entire products\n\n•\tProduct planning and customization, including integration into the overall system\n\n•\tRepair and testing activities, including directly at the customer's site\n\n*Your Profile*\n\n•\tDegree in mechatronics, mechanical engineering, automation technology\n\nor Technician qualification in mechatronics, mechanical engineering\n\nor Completed vocational training as an industrial mechanical\u002Fmechatronic technician with advanced knowledge\n\n•\tKnowledge of design \u002F CAD is essential\n\n•\tBasic knowledge of the Machinery Directive and the application of standards is an advantage\n\n•\tDesirable: basic knowledge of electrical engineering, electronics, circuits and automation\n\n•\tStructured way of working and initiative\n\n•\tEnjoy interdisciplinary cooperation\n\n•\tEnglish language skills spoken and written\n\n•\tProfessional experience is not necessarily required, but graduates with a focus on practical work are also an alternative (HandsOn mentality should be in the foreground)\n\n*Compensation, Benefits and Perks*\n\n•\tThe primary work location is Dresden, with the option for part-time home office based on individual arrangements\n\n•\tFrom 45,000€ annual pay\n\n•\t30 days of paid vacation\n\n•\tFull-time (37.5h) and part-time employment possible\n\n•\tBe part of an open and motivating work atmosphere where your ideas are valued\n\n•\tYou are welcome to contribute to the full mission, from tech details up to strategic decisions\n\n•\tThrive in a high-impact, flat-hierarchy working environment with fast decision-making\n\n•\tEmbark on a pioneering developer journey with limitless learning and growth opportunities\n\n*About HandsOn Robotics*\n\nHandsOn Robotics automates manual activities in industrial processes through the use of robot technology with the support of AI. Initially, our focus is on the automation of manual activities in large-scale catering. Filling jobs that are unattractive due to the physically strenuous, monotonous and repetitive tasks and low pay poses enormous challenges for our customers, which we meet with robot-supported automation products. Become part of the HandsOn Robotics team and help us to make the process in hospitals and university catering resilient and future-proof.\n\n*Apply now*\n\nIf you are ready to build a truly progressive automation company in the heart of Europe and want to play a key role in our team, we look forward to receiving your application! No matter if in German or English – please send us your CV, relevant work samples and optional recommendation letters to the following email address:\n\njobs@handson-robotics.de\n\nLooking forward to hearing from you!\n\nArt der Stelle: Vollzeit, Festanstellung\n\nGehalt: ab 45.000,00€ pro Jahr\n\nArbeitszeiten:\n* Montag bis Freitag\n\nArbeitsort: Vor Ort",
